WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:10.860
Tsuki no kaasu tsumetai yume no naka de

00:00.600 --> 00:10.860
Under the moon’s curse, inside of a cold dream…

00:19.240 --> 00:25.630
Kotoba no nai sekai de bokura wa ai wo kataru

00:19.240 --> 00:25.630
In a world without words, we speak of love

00:25.630 --> 00:29.840
itsuka kimi ni todoku made

00:25.630 --> 00:29.840
until it reaches you someday.

00:32.420 --> 00:39.310
Kizu darake no kaina de dakiyoseta kuchibiru no

00:32.420 --> 00:39.310
I want to melt the frozen over wish...

00:39.310 --> 00:45.140
haritsumeta negai tokashitakute

00:39.310 --> 00:45.140
from the lips that I embraced with arms covered in wounds.

00:45.230 --> 00:51.940
Nee, aishiatta kako no utsukushisa sutesareba

00:45.230 --> 00:51.940
Hey, if I abandon the beauty of the past when we loved each other,

00:52.320 --> 00:58.120
ashita motto kirei na yoru e yukeru kara

00:52.320 --> 00:58.120
then tomorrow, I can go to a more beautiful night.

00:58.490 --> 01:06.710
Tsuki no kaasu tsumetai yume no naka kara

00:58.490 --> 01:06.710
Under the moon’s curse, from inside of a cold dream.

01:06.710 --> 01:12.880
Kimi wo tooku tsuresaritakute

01:06.710 --> 01:12.880
I want to take you somewhere far away,

01:13.420 --> 01:16.760
doko made yukeru

01:13.420 --> 01:16.760
and go anywhere,

01:16.760 --> 01:24.980
ai wo shinjite ii basho made

01:16.760 --> 01:24.980
to a place where we can believe in love.

01:49.630 --> 01:51.160
I don't know when it started, but...

01:52.970 --> 01:56.100
Either I'm not able to sleep for nights...

01:56.100 --> 01:57.880
...or I'm sleeping all day.

02:02.980 --> 02:05.380
Why is my sleep messed up?

02:07.510 --> 02:15.280
Did this start when my
brother, Seimei, left me?

02:19.580 --> 02:20.790
Or...

02:22.660 --> 02:24.700
...is it because I met him?

02:28.330 --> 02:30.290
"I love you, Ritsuka..."

02:31.480 --> 02:33.190
I can't trust him.

02:33.760 --> 02:37.720
No matter what he says,
no matter what he does...

02:38.430 --> 02:41.720
He never tells me
anything I want to know.

02:50.430 --> 02:51.620
Soubi...

02:54.490 --> 02:58.140
I don't think I can sleep tonight again.

03:08.670 --> 03:10.630
What's up, Ritsuka?

03:11.130 --> 03:12.940
Just a little lack of sleep.

03:14.250 --> 03:15.280
Good morning.

03:18.080 --> 03:19.840
You didn't sleep much, either?

03:21.140 --> 03:22.430
Yuiko...

03:23.130 --> 03:25.470
I... I love Ritsuka!

03:26.430 --> 03:28.930
I will do anything for Ritsuka.

03:29.380 --> 03:30.560
I'll even die for him.

03:33.400 --> 03:34.860
Yayoi?

03:35.700 --> 03:38.320
I can't believe I couldn't
sleep because of that.

03:38.950 --> 03:40.820
I'll never give up!

03:41.870 --> 03:43.010
What was that?

03:43.450 --> 03:44.480
Who knows?

03:49.540 --> 03:52.320
I can't believe I overslept
just because I was worried about that.

03:53.670 --> 03:55.250
How old are you?

03:56.380 --> 03:57.910
W-What? How old?

03:57.910 --> 04:01.550
Me? U-Um, I'm 23.

04:01.550 --> 04:02.850
23!

04:03.930 --> 04:05.510
Pretty up there...

04:05.890 --> 04:08.180
I'm not interested in older people.

04:12.020 --> 04:14.230
Is everybody in need of sleep?

04:14.820 --> 04:15.870
How about you, Yuiko?

04:15.870 --> 04:16.770
Me?

04:17.360 --> 04:19.210
I'm fine.

04:19.210 --> 04:21.240
I sleep like a log every night!

04:21.490 --> 04:23.580
Okay! Listen up.

04:23.580 --> 04:28.010
Page 58, line 5. The author writes...

04:28.460 --> 04:31.520
Strawberries are delicious.

04:34.420 --> 04:36.670
I'm so full...

04:39.760 --> 04:43.570
Midori, you really have
a weird taste for drinks.

04:43.570 --> 04:44.380
Hmm?

04:44.680 --> 04:45.720
You think so?

04:45.720 --> 04:46.580
Yes.

04:47.020 --> 04:48.370
There are others.

04:48.370 --> 04:51.890
Summer tangelo coke, or melon
and watermelon juice mix...

04:52.140 --> 04:53.540
Yuck!

04:55.820 --> 04:59.460
But when we return to school,
we can't drink them anymore.

05:00.030 --> 05:01.650
That's fine with me.

05:01.820 --> 05:02.950
Why?

05:02.950 --> 05:04.610
Just 'cause.

05:09.790 --> 05:10.740
They're getting closer...

05:11.370 --> 05:12.220
Is it Soubi?

05:14.340 --> 05:15.080
No...

05:15.840 --> 05:17.860
It's not Soubi.

05:17.860 --> 05:19.840
It's someone a lot weaker than Soubi.

05:36.500 --> 05:38.200
They've already arrived.

05:39.110 --> 05:40.150
Yeah.

05:41.860 --> 05:43.610
Loveless and Soubi...

05:44.070 --> 05:45.280
What's going to happen to them?

05:48.410 --> 05:49.490
Who knows.

05:53.000 --> 05:54.610
They've gone.

05:55.710 --> 05:57.500
Say, Kin...

05:58.170 --> 06:00.590
I wonder if Soubi is powerful?

06:04.470 --> 06:06.380
You asked a bad question.

06:06.380 --> 06:07.970
Bad question?

06:08.600 --> 06:09.640
Yeah.

06:10.770 --> 06:13.100
He's perfect.

06:13.900 --> 06:18.730
Soubi's battle is on another level
because he can choose his attacks.

06:19.730 --> 06:21.900
He could physically inflict pain...

06:22.700 --> 06:25.070
...or mentally destroy you.

06:26.120 --> 06:28.720
Soubi doesn't have a weakness.

06:29.370 --> 06:30.450
What's that?

06:30.790 --> 06:35.120
The teacher thinks it's
a given for Soubi to win.

06:35.120 --> 06:37.160
That's kinda lame.

06:37.410 --> 06:38.750
Yeah.

06:40.050 --> 06:42.830
In any case, we'll find
out when we fight him.

06:46.090 --> 06:47.350
You can't sleep?

06:48.720 --> 06:50.840
But I do dream.

06:51.850 --> 06:53.010
What kind of dream?

06:54.020 --> 06:55.560
I don't remember...

06:56.190 --> 06:59.030
My current life is like a dream...

06:59.650 --> 07:04.960
I'm a two year old Ritsuka.
When the real Ritsuka wakes up...

07:06.740 --> 07:09.690
...the present me will disappear.

07:12.250 --> 07:13.470
Is that okay with you?

07:16.040 --> 07:17.830
Some time ago, you told me...

07:19.040 --> 07:22.490
...that you wanted to know what
really happened to your brother.

07:24.170 --> 07:26.990
If you disappear, you'll never know.

07:41.520 --> 07:44.750
The present you is reality, Ritsuka.

07:58.540 --> 08:00.870
Oh, cute!

08:01.670 --> 08:03.620
Right? Isn't it cute?

08:05.090 --> 08:08.380
Forget this. Let's
hurry up and find them.

08:08.970 --> 08:10.470
Come on.

08:10.470 --> 08:13.880
If it weren't for this, we
wouldn't be able to leave school.

08:14.230 --> 08:16.290
Well yes, but...

08:17.640 --> 08:19.080
Ew!

08:21.110 --> 08:22.370
Anything wrong?

08:23.520 --> 08:24.940
Calling me up all of a sudden like this...

08:31.240 --> 08:32.400
Never mind.

08:32.790 --> 08:33.660
Why?

08:35.450 --> 08:38.950
Cause, you're not gonna tell me anyway.

08:39.870 --> 08:41.870
Who knows until you ask me?

08:41.870 --> 08:44.320
Then I want the truth!

08:44.920 --> 08:46.850
Why did Seimei get killed?

08:49.130 --> 08:49.910
Fine...

08:58.270 --> 08:59.220
Kin!

09:00.060 --> 09:01.060
What's wrong?

09:01.730 --> 09:02.880
It's Soubi.

09:03.980 --> 09:06.320
There were no indications
of his presence earlier.

09:07.230 --> 09:09.190
What a fighting presence...

09:15.200 --> 09:17.530
The opponent will be here soon.

09:19.040 --> 09:22.540
If we fight, you'll find
out what you wanted to know.

09:23.920 --> 09:25.000
What will you do?

09:26.250 --> 09:27.720
I...

09:27.720 --> 09:29.290
Sentou system, on!

09:43.600 --> 09:46.780
Soubi Agatsuma and
Ritsuka Aoyagi, right?

09:46.780 --> 09:48.730
You want this, don't you, Loveless?

09:50.900 --> 09:54.110
What you want to know is written inside.

09:54.660 --> 09:57.370
I'm sure Soubi isn't
telling you anything, right?

09:58.330 --> 09:59.160
I declare...

09:59.160 --> 10:00.090
Wait!

10:01.370 --> 10:03.870
The sacrifice is a girl!

10:04.100 --> 10:07.010
Oh, are you concerned about me?

10:07.010 --> 10:10.840
Don't worry, I've never had
an injury that left a scar.

10:11.160 --> 10:12.140
I see...

10:12.720 --> 10:14.550
I'll avoid your face.

10:15.340 --> 10:18.050
But if I miss, I'm sorry.

10:18.760 --> 10:19.260
Kin!

10:19.890 --> 10:21.930
I declare this to be a battle of spells.

10:23.850 --> 10:24.850
We accept.

10:25.510 --> 10:26.730
K-Kin!

10:26.730 --> 10:28.390
Hurry! Defend!

10:28.940 --> 10:32.150
One hundred thousand arrows, pierce
the enemy as fast as the wind.

10:32.900 --> 10:33.520
D-Deflection!

10:38.110 --> 10:38.650
Ginka!

10:41.700 --> 10:42.710
Are you okay?

10:42.710 --> 10:43.500
I'm fine.

10:43.500 --> 10:45.670
I did avoid your face.

10:52.880 --> 10:54.350
You mock us.

10:54.350 --> 10:56.640
We'll take care of the brat first.

10:56.640 --> 10:57.380
Loveless?

10:57.650 --> 11:00.840
Soubi was perfect because of Seimei.

11:01.230 --> 11:05.100
There's no way I'd lose against a
sacrifice that doesn't share a name!

11:07.270 --> 11:08.200
It's okay...

11:09.110 --> 11:11.560
This will end quickly, don't worry.

11:12.070 --> 11:15.320
I want that envelope!

11:15.820 --> 11:18.280
I want to know why Seimei was killed!

11:30.710 --> 11:31.760
You better win...

11:43.770 --> 11:44.970
I am Kinka.

11:46.060 --> 11:47.610
I am Ginka.

11:48.520 --> 11:51.600
Our real name is Sleepless.

11:51.600 --> 11:53.910
One name for the both of us.

11:54.400 --> 11:57.450
To the two beasts
having different names...

11:57.450 --> 12:00.000
...see the darkness of the
night that doesn't sleep.

12:01.200 --> 12:03.610
Light! Tear the night into pieces!

12:04.500 --> 12:07.120
Invalid! Light doesn't
reach the darkness!

12:08.170 --> 12:12.870
Glittering particles of light, use
that strength and erode the night.

12:14.510 --> 12:19.560
Curtain of total darkness, wrap us up
and hide us from the beasts' eyes!

12:23.970 --> 12:28.140
Flames! Tear apart the black cloth and
reveal all to the broad daylight.

12:33.820 --> 12:36.360
Clouds! Erase all the stars!

12:36.360 --> 12:39.360
From the layers of dark clouds,
throw your lightning!

12:49.170 --> 12:51.290
Ginka! Are you okay?

12:51.790 --> 12:53.250
What kind of guy is he?

12:53.250 --> 12:56.290
Turning our spells
without first defending...

12:58.130 --> 13:01.420
You! Don't ridicule our spells like that!

13:01.740 --> 13:03.640
Enough petty tactics!

13:05.380 --> 13:10.220
Stars for darkness, lightning
for dark clouds, fire for cloth...

13:10.600 --> 13:13.470
It is standard to turn your opponent's strengths
back at him.

13:14.270 --> 13:16.280
Huh, such an honor student.

13:16.280 --> 13:19.110
No wonder you were the teacher's pet.

13:28.790 --> 13:29.930
He reacted?

13:31.000 --> 13:32.410
Yeah, but with what?

13:34.170 --> 13:36.870
Everybody learns the same way in school.

13:37.340 --> 13:38.530
Teacher's pet or not...

13:39.090 --> 13:40.130
...school is school.

13:41.260 --> 13:42.300
He...

13:54.480 --> 13:56.980
He praises me only
for self-satisfaction.

14:01.240 --> 14:01.860
Ginka?

14:04.370 --> 14:05.820
Hey, Soubi...

14:07.030 --> 14:11.280
Teacher taught us your weakness.

14:12.000 --> 14:13.330
How cruel...

14:13.330 --> 14:15.040
You were his star pupil, weren't you?

14:17.000 --> 14:18.460
Now, Kin!

14:20.550 --> 14:23.900
Restraint! Your body and
spirit will not be free!

14:25.550 --> 14:27.380
Yes! We restrained them!

14:36.610 --> 14:37.430
Soubi!

14:41.150 --> 14:44.360
Are you in more pain that I am?

14:47.410 --> 14:48.320
Ritsuka...

15:02.630 --> 15:03.460
Ritsuka!

15:05.380 --> 15:08.510
Hang in there, Soubi...

15:09.600 --> 15:11.840
Yes, master.

15:13.520 --> 15:14.420
Here he comes!

15:14.420 --> 15:15.930
Don't panic.

15:15.930 --> 15:18.230
When he tries to release the restraint...

15:17.520 --> 15:19.140
I won't release them.

15:20.070 --> 15:21.400
Not even necessary.

15:22.940 --> 15:26.840
Unrivaled. One that
will entirely overpower...

15:30.030 --> 15:32.330
K-Kin, defense!

15:32.330 --> 15:33.030
Y-Yeah!

15:33.750 --> 15:36.410
Invalid! Attack with full destructive force.

15:39.130 --> 15:41.290
Flame! Severe flames!

15:47.220 --> 15:49.540
I can barely stand...

15:50.970 --> 15:56.010
Is it because of the restraints?
Or is it because of Soubi?

16:02.190 --> 16:05.360
It must be Soubi's voice...

16:05.780 --> 16:09.570
Each flame! Use your full power
and tear the darkness apart!

16:18.910 --> 16:20.350
Sleepless...

16:21.630 --> 16:25.490
Your sleepless nights
don't amount to much.

16:46.740 --> 16:47.450
Here.

16:54.490 --> 16:55.540
Are you sure?

16:56.200 --> 16:59.830
There might be things you don't
want to talk about written in here.

17:02.040 --> 17:04.040
Do as you wish.

17:07.090 --> 17:07.630
Soubi!

17:14.720 --> 17:16.640
If you want a fistfight, that's fine.

17:26.110 --> 17:27.150
Kin!

17:28.860 --> 17:30.270
Done already?

17:32.320 --> 17:33.640
No!

17:37.290 --> 17:40.080
That's enough. Let them go.

17:40.710 --> 17:43.330
I don't like this! Please!

17:43.330 --> 17:45.410
Then you should command me.

17:48.420 --> 17:50.790
Use me as you please.

17:51.680 --> 17:53.800
Ritsuka, you are my law.

17:54.140 --> 17:55.630
That's it?

18:01.520 --> 18:03.590
The half that receives commands, and...

18:05.400 --> 18:07.300
...the half that gives commands.

18:09.280 --> 18:12.820
Is that all we are?

18:36.640 --> 18:38.050
Hey, wait.

18:43.270 --> 18:45.930
What does this mean?

18:46.360 --> 18:47.760
I don't know.

18:47.760 --> 18:50.320
The teacher just gave it to us.

18:50.320 --> 18:52.900
You should ask Soubi
when it comes to the teacher.

18:53.860 --> 18:55.930
If he answers, that is.

19:07.460 --> 19:09.200
Septimal Moon...

19:09.200 --> 19:10.990
Sentouki school.

19:11.380 --> 19:12.570
Teacher.

19:12.570 --> 19:14.420
Weird memo...

19:24.180 --> 19:25.720
I don't get it.

19:37.490 --> 19:40.110
Hey, I got some dinner!

19:41.910 --> 19:42.980
Thank you.

19:44.250 --> 19:46.960
But Soubi, you eat this kind of food?

19:46.960 --> 19:49.390
I wondered what they taste like.

19:49.790 --> 19:51.040
I see...

19:55.470 --> 19:57.750
Soubi, you've changed.

19:57.750 --> 19:58.870
You think so?

19:58.870 --> 20:00.750
You did.

20:00.750 --> 20:03.940
Is it, by any chance,
because of that brat...

20:08.980 --> 20:10.020
Excuse me.

20:10.940 --> 20:14.190
Hey, Soubi, this is a
pretty important topic.

20:15.280 --> 20:16.860
Are you listening, Soubi?

20:16.860 --> 20:18.110
Hey!

20:18.400 --> 20:20.280
Hey, Soubi!

20:20.990 --> 20:23.780
Hey, what is this treatment?

20:23.780 --> 20:25.330
Pervert! Molester!

20:25.340 --> 20:27.240
I'm gonna eat your food!

20:27.240 --> 20:31.710
<i>Go to bed already</i>

20:27.240 --> 20:31.710
<i>*Chuu* (Kiss)</i>

20:28.870 --> 20:31.150
I thought a mouse was crying.

20:35.050 --> 20:37.140
Thank you, Ritsuka.

20:44.770 --> 20:48.210
Soubi, I realized...

20:48.850 --> 20:53.470
This is a lot better than giving commands.

21:09.620 --> 21:14.470
I don't think I can sleep
again... because of you.

21:14.020 --> 21:17.000
MAIL NO. 001

21:14.020 --> 21:17.000
Subject: I Almost Forgot

21:14.020 --> 21:17.000
From: Soubi Agatsuma

21:14.020 --> 21:17.000
To: Ritsuka

21:14.020 --> 21:17.000
Kiss me

21:26.810 --> 21:29.210
Good night, Ritsuka.

21:29.930 --> 21:34.890
To be continued...

21:31.930 --> 21:41.480
Setsunasa no kagiri made dakishimete mo

21:31.930 --> 21:41.480
Even if I hold you with all my suffering,

21:42.280 --> 21:51.790
itsu made mo hitotsu ni wa narenakute

21:42.280 --> 21:51.790
we still can't be one.

21:52.370 --> 22:02.300
Yasashisa yori fukai basho de fureau no wa itami dake

21:52.370 --> 22:02.300
The only thing that we can feel deep within besides kindness is pain,

22:02.710 --> 22:10.300
futari wo musunde kudasai

22:02.710 --> 22:10.300
so please, bind the two of us together.

22:12.850 --> 22:17.690
Bokura wa mou yume wo minai

22:12.850 --> 22:17.690
We no longer dream anymore,

22:17.690 --> 22:22.820
tomadoinagara te wo totte

22:17.690 --> 22:22.820
when you're wavering, take my hand

22:23.110 --> 22:32.030
zankoku na yoake no hou e arukidasu

22:23.110 --> 22:32.030
as we tread towards the cruel light of dawn.

22:33.160 --> 22:43.170
Hontou no kotoba wa kitto hontou no sekai no dokoka

22:33.160 --> 22:43.170
I'm sure real words are somewhere in the real world.

22:43.500 --> 22:52.390
Bokura no mukuchi na yoru ni hisonderu

22:43.500 --> 22:52.390
They lurk in the shadows of our silent nights.

22:52.760 --> 22:57.890
Ima mo kitto

22:52.760 --> 22:57.890
Surely, even now...

23:00.980 --> 23:02.810
Ritsuka Aoyagi, age 12.

23:03.490 --> 23:07.580
He is convinced that his
present self is not the real him.

23:07.950 --> 23:09.360
The reason is...

23:09.360 --> 23:11.110
My mom has nothing to do with it.

23:11.410 --> 23:12.580
This injury is...

23:12.580 --> 23:14.120
Um, I just tripped...

23:14.120 --> 23:15.050
Does it hurt?

23:15.050 --> 23:16.090
Not at all.

23:16.090 --> 23:17.620
I know it hurts...

23:18.460 --> 23:20.370
Tale six, Painless.

23:21.130 --> 23:23.310
Hey, Ritsuka, let's have a date.

23:23.310 --> 23:24.020
What?
